{
  "_doc": "R3 §5a — the REVIEWED idle periodic timers per page (codex r3 P1-2, bound to reviewed SOURCE per codex r4 P1-2). Only these may stay pending while a page counts as SETTLED. Each entry BINDS: kind + delay + call site (enclosing function) + cbHash (sha256 of the callback's full whitespace-normalized source) + closureHash (sha256 over every page function the callback reaches by name). The harness exempts a timer only on an exact (kind, delay, cbHash) match of an entry whose closure is unchanged; ANY change → not exempt (blocks settling) and contract/idle-timers.guard.test.js is RED until re-reviewed (node contract/idle-timers.js --print <dir>). callback / at / executes / closure are for the reviewer; effects (the writes / network calls its execution closure reaches) must be [] — checked by the guard, so display-only is verified, not asserted. Each is DISPLAY-ONLY over data the page already holds — none writes or changes an order fact. Everything else blocks settling; a running callback is always awaited.",
